#: sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn:51
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`bun run cat security:gate`, before the site is built. It runs every security check the repository names: workflow injection, secret leaks, lockfile and toolchain pins, QA reviewer permission, materialised fixity, and third-party action SHA pinning outside staging-only workflows. Each reports pass, fail or unknown; a blocking fail or unknown refuses the publish."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn:75
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`compose-docs.ts` composes the docs layers into one Jekyll source (`cat-harness/docs/` as the base, the checkout root's `docs/` laid over it); then each layer that builds a site of its own composes it into that source at `<instance>/`, so the result is one site with one sidebar, search and language selector. The step is bound by the Tool, not by a `calledElement`: the step names skill `docs-generation`, each Tool that satisfies it and composes a site lists its own `subprocesses`, and those carry the steps; which layers compose a site is data in their declarations. A composing Tool may name a post-build pass, which `Task_Build` runs after the Jekyll build. With nothing to compose, the source is left as `compose-docs` wrote it, and that is reported."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn:59
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`passed` only on exit 0, meaning no blocking check failed or could not be run. Advisory findings (dependency advisories, staging-only pinning) never block, and they are not cleared either."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn:153
