msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn:82
#. Diagram label
msgid "Build the Jekyll site and the API reference"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Builds the composed source with Jekyll 4 and just-the-docs (`bundle exec jekyll build`), runs each composing Tool's post-build pass, mounts instance-rendered content (`mount-instance-docs.ts`), and generates the TypeScript API reference with TypeDoc (`.github/actions/typedoc-api`). The main deploy is a full build: every index is rebuilt from the tree being published. See skill `feature-staging`, section Build types."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn:16
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Builds the docs site from this checkout's sources and publishes it to `gh-pages` (`.github/workflows/docs-site.yml`). Publishing replaces `gh-pages` wholesale: anything on the branch that this build did not produce is gone unless restored, so the open pull requests' staging previews are copied in before the replace and checked on the deployed branch after it. The site is published whatever the built-site checks find: they run before the push and are judged after it, so a finding turns the run red with the site already live. A refused security gate or a failed deploy stops the run, and a check that could not tell counts as a failure (`ci-health`). Every failure, from a refused security gate to a lost preview or a failed check, goes through one alert to the publication manager, and the next clean publish closes it. Mechanical throughout; there is no human lane."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn:119
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Calls Process_RenderKgToCdn with the built tree, the site root as publication root URL, and GitHub Pages as target, so its `gh-pages` Tool (`publish-gh-pages.sh`) replaces the branch and returns the push's status and message. A status other than `pushed` takes `no` at Did the deploy succeed?."
msgstr ""

